Legal — please replace the questionnaire response with the following:

“Scaffold supports the SSO functionality currently shipped and documented for supported configurations. Scaffold accepts product feedback through its ordinary account and support channels and investigates reproducible defects in the Services through the applicable support process.

Product feedback and support discussions are informational and operational only. They do not create a roadmap review, product-prioritization, development, delivery, compatibility, or other future-functionality commitment.

Customer remains responsible for its identity provider, credentials, configurations, approvals, administrative permissions, and changes to its identity or permission model. Customer-side identity-provider or permission changes, unsupported configurations, and setup or implementation errors are addressed through ordinary support and reasonable configuration guidance only. They do not obligate Scaffold to maintain compatibility, modify the Services, provide an interim or custom administrative-role workaround, or absorb the operational consequences of those changes.”

Please do not include language that:

- Requires or implies a roadmap review, including one “within thirty (30) days”;
- Makes a customer identity or permission-model change trigger a contractual obligation;
- Promises an interim, custom, or alternative admin-role workaround;
- Commits Scaffold to preserve compatibility after customer-side changes;
- Requires Scaffold to review, prioritize, develop, deliver, or modify functionality;
- Makes Scaffold responsible for customer-side identity, permissions, credentials, approvals, configuration, or implementation changes; or
- Creates credits, service levels, renewal rights, or other remedies tied to those issues.

This keeps the answer limited to shipped SSO, ordinary product feedback, and reproducible platform-defect support without turning the questionnaire into a roadmap or administrative-entitlement commitment.

