The addendum text wasn’t included, so I’d replace the relevant security, support, connector, retention/deletion, and future-change language with the following:

Proposed replacement language

Security, SSO, Connectors, Support, and Product Feedback

Scaffold supports the SSO functionality currently made generally available and documented for supported configurations. Scaffold documents the then-current supported behavior, configurations, and applicable limitations of its connectors. Scaffold investigates reproducible defects in the Services through its ordinary support and defect-remediation processes in accordance with the applicable Support Policy.

Customer is responsible for its identity provider, credentials, access controls, configurations, approvals, administrative permissions, source systems, connector configuration, and changes to its identity, permission, or connector-support model. Scaffold will provide ordinary support and reasonable configuration guidance for supported configurations. Customer-side changes, unsupported configurations, and setup or implementation issues do not require Scaffold to modify the Services, preserve compatibility after such changes, provide a custom or interim connector or administrative-role workaround, map Customer-specific permissions, or absorb the operational consequences of those changes.

Retention and deletion of Customer Data will be handled in accordance with the applicable Agreement, Data Processing Addendum, Documentation, and standard service controls. No customer-specific retention period, deletion configuration, bespoke deletion workflow, or other customer-specific data-lifecycle control is included unless expressly agreed in a written Order Form or other written amendment signed by both parties.

Scaffold may receive and capture account and product feedback through its ordinary account, support, and product channels. Such feedback and related discussions are informational and operational only. They do not constitute a roadmap review or create any commitment regarding product prioritization, development, modification, delivery, timing, compatibility, future functionality, service levels, credits, renewal rights, or other remedies.

For clarity, this language confirms support for currently shipped and documented functionality and ordinary support for reproducible platform defects. It does not require Scaffold to provide future functionality, maintain compatibility with future customer-side identity or administrative-model changes, provide a custom connector or administrative workaround, or assume responsibility for customer-side configuration, permission, identity-provider, source-system, or implementation changes.

Redline cleanup

Delete or replace any language that:

- Requires a roadmap review or response within a specified period;
- Requires Scaffold to assess, prioritize, develop, deliver, or modify functionality;
- Promises a customer-specific retention or deletion configuration;
- Requires a bespoke deletion workflow or data-lifecycle control;
- Promises a custom, interim, or alternative connector workaround;
- Requires customer-specific administrative-role mapping or permission design;
- Guarantees compatibility after a customer changes its identity provider, permission model, source system, or connector configuration;
- Makes Scaffold responsible for customer credentials, approvals, configurations, permissions, source systems, or implementation;
- Creates an SLA, credit, renewal right, or other remedy for those matters; or
- States or implies that Scaffold will absorb future identity, permission, connector, or administrative-model changes.

This keeps the answer affirmative: we support what is shipped and documented, investigate platform defects through normal support, document connector behavior, and capture product feedback—without converting those commitments into a roadmap, bespoke configuration, workaround, or future-change obligation.
